WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.356
- We've made tap handles for

00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:05.659
Budweiser, Goose Island, Miller Lite.

00:00:05.659 --> 00:00:07.253
You know, I think this is a first

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:10.202
with an actual snow
globe on the tap handle.

00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:11.763
Yee-Haw Pale Ale.

00:00:11.763 --> 00:00:14.328
I like this one because it's just a big,

00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:16.264
awesome-looking tap handle.

00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:20.516
Stiegl, Prescott, and Central
Waters, to name a few.

00:00:20.516 --> 00:00:24.709
I'm Mark Steinhardt, General
Manager of AJS Tap Handles.

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:27.459
I definitely would try that beer.

00:00:30.803 --> 00:00:32.763
So, a guy walks into a bar,

00:00:32.763 --> 00:00:35.399
and the first thing he does, if it's me,

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:37.363
I look what's on tap.

00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:41.228
Certainly, the unique tap
handles pique your interest

00:00:41.228 --> 00:00:43.859
and might push you to try that beer.

00:00:43.859 --> 00:00:47.503
I like this tap handle,
because I'm a road biker.

00:00:47.503 --> 00:00:50.189
We're located in Random Lake, Wisconsin,

00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:53.381
which is about 45 minutes
north of Milwaukee.

00:00:53.381 --> 00:00:56.098
Even though Wisconsin is a rural state,

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:58.540
we produce tap handles
for the mega-breweries

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.373
on down to the smallest microbrew.

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:05.970
We believe we're the
largest domestic producer

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.037
of tap handles here in the U.S.

00:01:08.037 --> 00:01:09.946
We ship out approximately

00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:12.338
a half a million tap handles each year.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.687
We can produce the tap
handle from start to finish.

00:01:15.687 --> 00:01:17.548
This is a very detailed tap handle,

00:01:17.548 --> 00:01:20.135
and I would guess takes about an hour

00:01:20.135 --> 00:01:23.444
to hand paint all the detail on it.

00:01:23.444 --> 00:01:27.983
Companies do try to have
the most eye-catching,

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.766
most unique tap handle in the bar.

00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:35.136
And it is a cross between
art and manufacturing.

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:38.469
We always say our tap handle
will sell your first beer,

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:41.219
and your beer will sell the rest.

